siness accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1958140/000110465926058558/0001104659-26-058558-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-058558"}],"bear":[{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-57.3% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1958140/000110465926058558/0001104659-26-058558-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-058558"},{"text":"Debt of $709.2m against equity of $519.0m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1958140/000110465926058558/0001104659-26-058558-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-058558"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 3.8% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (140,398 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1958140/000080724926000022/0000807249-26-000022-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 26.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.26,"consecutive":2,"current":0.525,"current_display":"52.5%","threshold_display":"26.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":0.017,"current_display":"1.7%","thres